{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Pair group rotation: the 2603 mechanism for ABJM pairs (2026-10-12)\n\n**Status: NOT RUN in Wolfram.** The shared kernel died and the Wolfram Engine licence expired while this notebook was written. Every code cell is an *unrun port* of the python computation in the scratchpad (`.../scratchpad/pairgroup/py/*.py`, summary `RESULTS.md`); the python results are pasted in the markdown cell **under** each code cell (tag: [python exact] = Fractions/sympy, [python numeric] = complex128). Rerun top to bottom in VS Code after renewing the licence. All symbols are prefixed `pg`. Cell 10 (untwisting) builds full 256-dim matrices; the L = 3 options are slow.\n\nGoal (NEXT.md 2i): a 2603-type *common* group rotation of the first ABJM pair (A by $D=1-\\kappa\\Lambda$, F by $D^{-T}$), produced by localising transfer matrices on the non-good reference $\\langle W_a^L|$, so that pair 1 becomes $W_{a'}$, $a'=a(1-\\kappa z_4)/(1-\\kappa z_1)$.\n\n**Bottom line.**\n1. Derivation (2603 App. K transplanted): a column-support lemma. The rows $I$ of the $\\wedge^k$ auxiliary space with $1\\notin I$, $4\\in I$ are diagonal on both vacua, so the rest of the chain is transparent on them. Pair 1 localises $t_1(\\theta_F)$, $\\hat t_3(\\theta_A-h)$ for any geometry and **$t_2(\\theta_F+h)$ only at the ABJM point $\\theta_A-\\theta_F=2h$**, for any twist and any global rotation; the action equals $\\lambda_k\\times$ the 1-pair-chain transfer matrix.\n2. The localised algebra on pair 1 is 5-dimensional: $\\{1,X_1,X_2,X_3,X_3X_1\\}$ (4-dim off the ABJM point). It contains **no common group rotation** for a generic reference. The naive F-site dictionary ($M_2$, $M_3$) does not exist: the $\\wedge^k$ structure lives on the pair.\n3. On $\\langle W_a^L|$ the cyclic space per pair is 6-dim for $z_2\\neq z_3$ (fails, exact rank 5 vs 6) and 5-dim for $z_2=z_3$. **At the ABJM point with $z_2=z_3=y$ the common rotation exists as an exact 5-word formula**, $a$-independent and local (verified exactly at L = 2 and 3 pairs):\n$$K_\\kappa=s^2+\\kappa s\\Big(\\tfrac{X_1}{h^2\\lambda_1}+\\tfrac{X_2}{2h^4y\\lambda_2}+\\tfrac{X_3}{6h^5y^2\\lambda_3}\\Big)+\\kappa^2\\tfrac{X_3X_1}{24h^7y^2\\lambda_1\\lambda_3},\\quad s=1-\\kappa(z_1+z_4),$$\n$$\\langle W_a^L|K_\\kappa=(1-\\kappa z_1)^2\\langle W_{a'}\\otimes W_a^{L-1}|,$$\nwith $X_1=t_1(\\theta_2)$, $X_2=t_2(\\theta_2+h)$, $X_3=\\hat t_3(\\theta_2+h)$.\n4. Untwisting ($z=1+\\varepsilon\\phi$ with $\\phi_2=\\phi_3$): $K(\\tau)\\langle W^L|\\Psi\\rangle/(1-\\kappa z_1)^2$ converges like $O(\\varepsilon)$ to the even-bridge structure constants $\\langle \\mathrm{vac}\\otimes W_{-1}^{L-1}|\\Psi_0\\rangle$ ($\\kappa=1/z_4$) and $\\langle \\mathrm{vac}^{L-1}\\otimes W_{-1}|\\Psi_0\\rangle$ ($\\kappa\\to1$, $a'-a=-1$, HW trick). Checked on all HW states at L = 2 and 3 pairs [python numeric].",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "> **Rerun status, 2026-10-13:** all code cells now run in the live kernel and carry native outputs (the 'NOT RUN' banner above is historical). Reproduced: sections 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 5b, 6, 7 (L = 2), 8, 9 (L = 2). **One discrepancy** (section 5: constant of four product words is not $\\prod\\lambda_k$, only proportional). **Skipped as too heavy: L = 3 in sections 7 and 9.** Cells 11 and 14 take about 4.6 min and 3 min. Details in the notes under each cell and in `notes/rerun-2026-10-13.md`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 0. Setup\n\nConventions as in `ABJM-3pt-transfer-matrices.md`. Chain A F A F ...; bras are row vectors (`psi . M`); $\\rho_A(E_{ab})=e_{ab}$, $\\rho_F(E_{ab})=-e_{ba}$; $T=L_1\\cdots L_N G$.\n\nFused transfer matrices for all $k$ in one single-pass form: $t_k(u)=\\prod_s g_s(u)\\,\\mathrm{tr}[L^{(k)}_1\\cdots L^{(k)}_N\\,\\wedge^kG]$ with $L^{(k)}_s=(u-\\tilde\\theta_s)+h\\sum_{ab}D_k(e_{ab})\\otimes\\rho_s(E_{ab})$. Here $D_k$ is the derivation action on $\\wedge^k\\mathbb C^4$ (from `Minors`), $\\tilde\\theta_A=\\theta$, $\\tilde\\theta_F=\\theta+(k-1)h$, $g_A=\\prod_{j=1}^{k-1}(u-\\theta-jh)$ and $g_F=\\prod_{j=0}^{k-2}(u-\\theta-jh)$. For $k=2,3$ this reproduces the forms of `dual-lax-t3.wb`.\n\n`reg -> True` gives $\\hat t_k$: exactly vanishing scalar factors $(u-\\theta-jh)=0$ are dropped. `pgLam[k,u,thRest]` is the localisation constant $\\lambda_k$ (pairs 2..L, zero factors dropped). `pgTdef` builds the quantum-minor definition, used for calibration.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pgh = 1/2;\npgId4 = IdentityMatrix[4, SparseArray];\npgE[i_, j_] := SparseArray[{{i, j} -> 1}, {4, 4}];\npgRho[\"A\"][a_, b_] := pgE[a, b];\npgRho[\"F\"][a_, b_] := -pgE[b, a];\npgD[k_] := pgD[k] = Module[{eps}, Table[D[Minors[IdentityMatrix[4] + eps Normal[pgE[a, b]], k], eps] /. eps -> 0, {a, 4}, {b, 4}]];\npgThT[ty_, k_, t_] := If[ty == \"A\", t, t + (k - 1) pgh];\npgDropZeros[fs_List] := DeleteCases[fs, x_ /; TrueQ[x == 0]];\npgGfac[ty_, k_, u_, t_, reg_] := Module[{fs},\n   fs = If[ty == \"A\", Table[u - t - j pgh, {j, 1, k - 1}], Table[u - t - j pgh, {j, 0, k - 2}]];\n   Times @@ If[TrueQ[reg], pgDropZeros[fs], fs]];\npgLax[k_, ty_, u_, t_] := Module[{n = Binomial[4, k]},\n   Table[(u - pgThT[ty, k, t]) KroneckerDelta[i, j] pgId4 + pgh Sum[pgD[k][[a, b, i, j]] pgRho[ty][a, b], {a, 4}, {b, 4}], {i, n}, {j, n}]];\npgT[k_, u_, types_, th_, G_, reg_: False] := Module[{n = Binomial[4, k], mon, lx, wG, pref},\n   If[k == 0, Return[IdentityMatrix[4^Length[types], SparseArray]]];\n   mon = pgLax[k, types[[1]], u, th[[1]]];\n   Do[lx = pgLax[k, types[[s]], u, th[[s]]];\n    mon = Table[Sum[KroneckerProduct[mon[[i, m]], lx[[m, j]]], {m, n}], {i, n}, {j, n}], {s, 2, Length[types]}];\n   wG = Minors[G, k];\n   pref = Times @@ Table[pgGfac[types[[s]], k, u, th[[s]], reg], {s, Length[types]}];\n   pref Sum[mon[[i, j]] wG[[j, i]], {i, n}, {j, n}]];\npgUV[i_] := UnitVector[4, i];\npgProd[vs_List] := Flatten[Fold[KroneckerProduct, First[vs], Rest[vs]]];\npgW[a_] := {pgUV[1] + a pgUV[4], pgUV[4] - a pgUV[1]};\npgSplit[psi_, rest_] := Module[{m = ArrayReshape[Normal[psi], {16, Length[rest]}], p},\n   p = (m . rest)/(rest . rest); {p, m - Outer[Times, p, rest]}];\npgLocalQ[psi_, rest_] := Module[{s = pgSplit[psi, rest]}, AllTrue[Flatten[s[[2]]], TrueQ[# == 0] &] && ! AllTrue[s[[1]], TrueQ[# == 0] &]];\npgLam[k_, u_, thRest_List] := Times @@ pgDropZeros[Flatten[Table[If[OddQ[s], Table[u - thRest[[s]] - j pgh, {j, 0, k - 1}],\n       Join[{u - thRest[[s]] - k pgh}, Table[u - thRest[[s]] - j pgh, {j, 0, k - 2}]]], {s, Length[thRest]}]]];\npgMon1[u_, types_, th_, G_] := Module[{mon = pgLax[1, types[[1]], u, th[[1]]], lx},\n   Do[lx = pgLax[1, types[[s]], u, th[[s]]]; mon = Table[Sum[KroneckerProduct[mon[[i, m]], lx[[m, j]]], {m, 4}], {i, 4}, {j, 4}], {s, 2, Length[types]}];\n   Table[Sum[mon[[i, m]] G[[m, j]], {m, 4}], {i, 4}, {j, 4}]];\npgTdef[k_, u_, types_, th_, G_] := Module[{ts = Table[pgMon1[u - m pgh, types, th, G], {m, 0, k - 1}]},\n   Sum[Sum[Signature[p] (Dot @@ Table[ts[[m, ss[[p[[m]]]], ss[[m]]]], {m, k}]), {p, Permutations[Range[k]]}], {ss, Subsets[Range[4], {k}]}]];\npgG0 = {{3/2, -1/3, 2, 1/5}, {1, 2/7, -1, 3}, {-2/3, 1, 1/2, 1}, {1/4, -1, 5/3, -2}};\npgV0 = {1, 2, -1, 3}; pgU0 = {2, 1/2, 1, 1}; pgU0 = pgU0 - (pgV0 . pgU0)/(pgV0 . pgV0) pgV0;\npgApplyWord[w_, psi_, types_, th_, G_] := Fold[#1 . pgT[#2[[1]], #2[[2]], types, th, G, True] &, psi, w];",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. Calibration: single-pass fused $t_k$ vs quantum minors ($k=1..4$)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pgCal = Table[{k, Max[Abs[Flatten[Normal[pgT[k, 37/100, {\"A\", \"F\"}, {2/7, -3/5}, pgG0] - pgTdef[k, 37/100, {\"A\", \"F\"}, {2/7, -3/5}, pgG0]]]]]}, {k, 1, 4}];\nGrid[Prepend[pgCal, {\"k\", \"max |fused single-pass t_k - quantum-minor t_k| (exact, 1 pair, random twist)\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
