      {
       "data": "Out[25]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{formula holds for all (j,k)} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{zero pattern of <e1 e4|(L\\_A L\\_F)\\_jk(u)} & \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{0 at u=thF} & \\text{0 at u=thF} & \\text{0 at u=thF} & \\text{*}\\\\\\hline\\text{0} & \\text{0 at u=thA} & \\text{0} & \\text{0 at u=thA}\\\\\\hline\\text{0} & \\text{0} & \\text{0 at u=thA} & \\text{0 at u=thA}\\\\\\hline\\text{0} & \\text{0} & \\text{0} & \\text{0 at u=thA}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "4d8ca87d-8053-424b-a6cb-d6e010117c3c"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python result** (`pairvac_pattern.py`, sympy, exact): the formula holds for all $(j,k)$. The off-diagonal entries $(2,1),(3,1),(4,1),(3,2),(4,2),(4,3)$ **and $(2,3)$** vanish identically. The extra zeros are $(2,4),(3,4)$ (and $(2,2),(3,3),(4,4)$) at $u=\\theta_A$, and $(1,2),(1,3)$ (and $(1,1)$) at $u=\\theta_F$. Only $(1,4)$ never vanishes; it carries the singlet $-h^2\\langle S|$.\n\n**Derivation (column-support lemma, the 2603 App. K argument for this chain).** In the $\\wedge^k$ auxiliary space, row $I$ of $\\langle e_1|L^{(k)}_A$ is off-diagonal only if $1\\in I$. Row $I$ of $\\langle e_4|L^{(k)}_F$ is off-diagonal only if $4\\notin I$. So on $D_k=\\{I: 1\\notin I,\\ 4\\in I\\}$ every vacuum site is diagonal, with $I$-independent eigenvalues $(u-\\tilde\\theta_A)$ and $(u-\\tilde\\theta_F-h)$. If the Lax product of pair 1 at $u_0$ has column support inside $D_k$, the index stays in $D_k$ through pairs $2..L$, and the twist only closes the trace. Hence\n$$\\langle\\mathrm{vac}^L|t_k(u_0)=\\lambda_k(u_0)\\,\\langle\\mathrm{vac}_{\\rm pair}|t_k^{(1\\,\\rm pair)}(u_0)\\otimes\\langle \\mathrm{vac}^{L-1}|$$\nfor every twist, and by $GL(4)$ covariance on every global rotation of the vacuum (no goodness condition). The F site at $u_0=\\tilde\\theta_F$ removes all columns without 4. The A site at $u_0=\\theta_A-h$ removes all columns containing 1. So:\n- $k=1$: $t_1(\\theta_F)$ works for any geometry;\n- $k=3$: $\\hat t_3(\\theta_A-h)$ works for any geometry;\n- $k=2$: both conditions are needed, $\\theta_F+h=\\theta_A-h$, i.e. **$\\theta_A-\\theta_F=2h$, the ABJM point**.\n\nThe constant is $\\lambda_k(u)=\\prod_{n\\ge2}\\prod_{j=0}^{k-1}(u-\\theta_{A,n}-jh)\\,(u-\\theta_{F,n}-kh)\\prod_{j=0}^{k-2}(u-\\theta_{F,n}-jh)$. Products localise if each factor's own condition holds when it acts; $t_1(\\theta_F)$ needs only the F site of pair 1 in its vacuum.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Which single $t_k(\\theta_F+mh)$ localise on pair 1, by geometry $d=(\\theta_A-\\theta_F)/h$\n\nSetup: 4 sites, random rational twist `pgG0`, random BPS reference $(v\\otimes u)^2$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pgScanD = Table[Module[{thF = -3/5, th, ref, rest, hits = {}},\n    th = {thF + d pgh, thF, 13/16, -5/16};\n    ref = pgProd[{pgV0, pgU0, pgV0, pgU0}]; rest = pgProd[{pgV0, pgU0}];\n    Do[Module[{out = ref . pgT[k, thF + m pgh, {\"A\", \"F\", \"A\", \"F\"}, th, pgG0, True]},\n      If[pgLocalQ[out, rest], AppendTo[hits, \"t\" <> ToString[k] <> \"(thF\" <> If[m >= 0, \"+\", \"\"] <> ToString[m] <> \"h)\"]]], {k, 1, 3}, {m, -2, 4}];\n    {d, Row[hits, \", \"]}], {d, -2, 4}];\nGrid[Prepend[pgScanD, {\"d = (thA - thF)/h\", \"single t_k(thF + m h) localising on pair 1\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"725118\" data-output-id=\"217\" data-out-n=\"28\" data-sub-idx=\"1\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"10\" data-sub-start=\"6\" data-sub-end=\"6\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[28]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"24\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:9.64em;vertical-align:-4.55em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.09em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:9.6em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-4.55em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">d = (thA - thF)/h</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.81em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">