span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.4461em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">16</span><span class=\"mspace mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1952em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.03148em;\">k</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">$673</span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8913em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.931em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.4811em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.2737em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:7.0474em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.2737em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.7737em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.0511em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.7737em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.5422em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.7737em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.0334em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.7737em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.2334em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.7737em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.5474em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.7737em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.2737em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[41]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{c0 (word 1)} & \\left(kap\\$6730\\,z1\\$6730+kap\\$6730\\,z4\\$6730-1\\right)^2\\\\\\hline\\text{c1 (X1 = t1(thF))} & -4\\,kap\\$6730\\,\\left(kap\\$6730\\,z1\\$6730+kap\\$6730\\,z4\\$6730-1\\right)\\\\\\hline\\text{c2 (X2 = t2(thF+h))} & -\\frac{8\\,kap\\$6730\\,\\left(kap\\$6730\\,z1\\$6730+kap\\$6730\\,z4\\$6730-1\\right)}{y\\$6730}\\\\\\hline\\text{c3 (X3 = t3\\^{}(thF+h))} & -\\frac{16\\,kap\\$6730\\,\\left(kap\\$6730\\,z1\\$6730+kap\\$6730\\,z4\\$6730-1\\right)}{3\\,y\\$6730^2}\\\\\\hline\\text{c4 (X3 X1)} & \\frac{16\\,kap\\$6730^2}{3\\,y\\$6730^2}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "9b1f68ec-17ac-44af-b778-7b103d65fcaa"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python result** (`pair_solve.py`, sympy, symbolic $z_1,y,z_4,h,a,\\kappa$): a unique solution, independent of $a$:\n$$c_0=(1-\\kappa(z_1+z_4))^2,\\ c_1=\\frac{\\kappa(1-\\kappa(z_1+z_4))}{h^2},\\ c_2=\\frac{\\kappa(1-\\kappa(z_1+z_4))}{2h^4y},\\ c_3=\\frac{\\kappa(1-\\kappa(z_1+z_4))}{6h^5y^2},\\ c_4=\\frac{\\kappa^2}{24h^7y^2}.$$\nIn normalised operators: $K=s^2+\\kappa s(2x_1-x_2/y+2x_3/y^2)+\\kappa^2x_3x_1/y^2$. It acts on W-pairs as $(1-\\kappa z_1)(1-\\kappa z_4)\\rho_{\\rm pair}(1-\\kappa\\Lambda)$; on weight state $(1,4)$ the eigenvalue is $(s+\\kappa z_4)^2=(1-\\kappa z_1)^2$.\n\nWhy it fails for $z_2\\neq z_3$: on $W_a$, $X_1$ produces the zero-weight junk $\\propto E_{22}+E_{33}$ and $X_2$ produces $\\propto z_3E_{22}+z_2E_{33}$. They cancel only if $z_2=z_3$; otherwise the cyclic space of $W_a$ on the pair is 6-dim against 5 localised directions.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. Full-chain exact check and locality: $\\langle W_a^L|K_\\kappa=(1-\\kappa z_1)^2\\langle W_{a'}\\otimes W_a^{L-1}|$\n\nSet `pgLp = 3` for the 6-site locality check (python: 32 s per transfer-matrix application; slower here, since it builds sparse 4096-dim matrices).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pgLp = 2;\npgVerify = Module[{thFs = Take[{-3/5, -11/8, -7/9}, pgLp], th, types, y = 5/4, z, G, l1, l2, l3, u1, u2, t1m, t2m, t3m},\n   th = Flatten[{# + 1, #} & /@ thFs]; types = Flatten[Table[{\"A\", \"F\"}, pgLp]];\n   z = {3/2, y, y, 4/7}; G = DiagonalMatrix[z];\n   u1 = th[[2]]; u2 = th[[2]] + pgh;\n   l1 = pgLam[1, u1, Drop[th, 2]]; l2 = pgLam[2, u2, Drop[th, 2]]; l3 = pgLam[3, u2, Drop[th, 2]];\n   t1m = pgT[1, u1, types, th, G]; t2m = pgT[2, u2, types, th, G]; t3m = pgT[3, u2, types, th, G, True];\n   Flatten[Table[Module[{ref = pgProd[Flatten[Table[pgW[a], pgLp], 1]], x1, x2, x3, x31},\n      x1 = Normal[ref . t1m]; x2 = Normal[ref . t2m]; x3 = Normal[ref . t3m]; x31 = Normal[x3 . t1m];\n      Table[Module[{s = 1 - kap (z[[1]] + z[[4]]), kw, ap, tgt},\n        kw = s^2 ref + kap s (x1/(pgh^2 l1) + x2/(2 pgh^4 y l2) + x3/(6 pgh^5 y^2 l3)) + kap^2 x31/(24 pgh^7 y^2 l1 l3);\n        ap = a (1 - kap z[[4]])/(1 - kap z[[1]]);\n        tgt = (1 - kap z[[1]])^2 pgProd[Join[pgW[ap], Flatten[Table[pgW[a], pgLp - 1], 1]]];\n        {a, kap, ap, kw == tgt}], {kap, {3/10, -7/5, 1/z[[4]]}}]], {a, {1/3, -1}}], 1]];\nGrid[Prepend[pgVerify, {\"a\", \"kappa\", \"a'\", \"<W_a^L| K = (1 - kappa z1)^2 <W_a' (x) W_a^(L-1)|  (exact)\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
