       "data": "Out[44]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{a} & \\text{kappa} & \\text{a'} & \\text{<W\\_a\\^{}L| K = (1 - kappa z1)\\^{}2 <W\\_a' (x) W\\_a\\^{}(L-1)|  (exact)}\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{116}{231} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{7}{5} & \\frac{6}{31} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{7}{4} & 0 & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline-1 & \\frac{3}{10} & -\\frac{116}{77} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline-1 & -\\frac{7}{5} & -\\frac{18}{31} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline-1 & \\frac{7}{4} & 0 & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "746d3834-96d3-48f4-94b9-c811996b7c44"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python result** (`word_verify.py 2`, `word_verify.py 3`, exact Fractions). Point: $h=1/2$, $\\theta_F=(-3/5,-11/8,-7/9)$, $\\theta_A=\\theta_F+2h$, $z=(3/2,5/4,5/4,4/7)$. The difference vector is **identically zero** in all 10 cases at both lengths:\n\n| L | $\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2,\\lambda_3$ | (a, κ) checked | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | −99/1600, −55539/2560000, −40851459/4096000000 | (1/3, 3/10), (1/3, −7/5), (1/3, 7/4 → a′=0), (−1, 2/9), (−1, 7/4 → a′=0) | exact |\n| 3 | −11803/720000, 3904467809/3110400000000, −48448411332167/139968000000000000 | same | exact |\n\n**Locality holds.** The coefficient structure is identical at L = 2 and 3; only $\\lambda_k$ changes, through the universal product formula.\n\nOverlap formula, for any joint eigenvector:\n$$\\langle W_{a'}\\otimes W_a^{L-1}|\\Psi\\rangle=\\frac{K_\\kappa(\\tau)}{(1-\\kappa z_1)^2}\\langle W_a^L|\\Psi\\rangle .$$\nAt $\\kappa=1/z_4$ this becomes the one-pair even bridge\n$$\\langle \\mathrm{vac}\\otimes W_a^{L-1}|\\Psi\\rangle=\\frac{z_1^2-z_1\\Sigma+\\Pi}{(z_1-z_4)^2}\\langle W_a^L|\\Psi\\rangle,\\quad \\Sigma=2x_1-x_2/y+2x_3/y^2,\\ \\Pi=x_3x_1/y^2$$\n(eigenvalues, $x_k$ normalised by $\\lambda_k$ as above).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Rerun 2026-10-13 (Wolfram).** Section 7 at L = 2 (`pgLp = 2`, 4 sites): $\\langle W_a^L|K_\\kappa=(1-\\kappa z_1)^2\\langle W_{a'}\\otimes W_a^{L-1}|$ holds exactly (True) for all 6 pairs $(a,\\kappa)\\in\\{1/3,-1\\}\\times\\{3/10,-7/5,1/z_4\\}$, including $\\kappa=1/z_4$ ($a'=0$). The $\\lambda_{1,2,3}$ of the table for L = 2 are reproduced (cell 17 prints $-99/1600$, $-55539/2560000$, $-40851459/4096000000$). The symbolic pair solution (cell 23) gives exactly $c_0=s^2$, $c_1=\\kappa s/h^2$, $c_2=\\kappa s/(2h^4y)$, $c_3=\\kappa s/(6h^5y^2)$, $c_4=\\kappa^2/(24h^7y^2)$ at $h=1/2$.\n\n**SKIPPED (too heavy), L = 3 (`pgLp = 3`, 6 sites, 4096-dim):** one 6-site `pgT[1, ...]` did not finish in 300 s and pushed MemoryInUse to about 7.5 GB (the port builds the monodromy by dense-ish `KroneckerProduct` of sparse blocks; python took 32 s per application). The L = 3 half of the claim ('verified exactly at L = 2 and 3 pairs') is therefore **not reproduced in this rerun**. A port that applies $t_k$ to the vector (site by site) instead of building the matrix would be needed.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "*(cell 23 note, 2026-10-13)* Section 6 (`pgPairSol`) and section 5b (cell 20) reproduced: $X_1=2h^2e_1\\otimes e_4G-h^2G_{41}S$ (entries $\\tfrac14g_{41}$, $\\tfrac12 g_{4j}$, $-\\tfrac14 g_{41}$ on the diagonal), $X_2$ has column 1 zero and entries $\\tfrac18\\times$ 2x2 minors of rows {2,4}/{3,4}, and $X_3=12h^5\\,(e_1\\,\\mathrm{cof}\\,G)\\otimes e_4$ (checked separately: True for the numeric twist `pgG0`).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 8. Negative controls (exact ranks, 4 sites)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
