   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python result** (`untwist.py 2`, `untwist.py 3`, complex128). All twisted states are non-degenerate and their overlap with the untwisted state tends to 1. $|$RHS − LHS$|\\le10^{-6}$; this is machine cancellation, since $K/N\\sim10^8$ while $\\langle W^L|\\Psi\\rangle\\sim10^{-10}$, and the identity is exact at finite twist. Errors $|$RHS − target$|$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-2},10^{-3},10^{-4}$ (all $O(\\varepsilon)$):\n\n| L | state(s) | target | mode vac | mode shift |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | singlet E=20 | $-1/\\sqrt{40}=-0.158114$ | 1.6e-3 / 1.6e-4 / 1.6e-5 | 5.2e-4 / 5.3e-5 / 5.3e-6 |\n| 2 | singlet E=4 | $1/\\sqrt{24}=0.204124$ | 2.0e-3 / 2.0e-4 / 2.0e-5 | 7.0e-4 / 6.8e-5 / 6.8e-6 |\n| 2 | [1,0,1] pair | 0 | 5.4e-3 / 5.4e-4 / 5.4e-5 | 3.1e-3 / 3.1e-4 / 3.1e-5 |\n| 2 | vacuum | 1 | 3e-13 / 3e-11 / 1e-8 | 4e-12 / 2e-10 / 7e-8 |\n| 3 | [1,0,1] (6 states) | −0.153484 (×2), −0.035872 ∓ 0.028637i, −0.171126, −0.027138 | ≤ 1.5e-3 / 3.8e-4 / 3.8e-5 | ≤ 3.8e-3 / 3.8e-4 / 3.8e-5 |\n| 3 | other 19 non-vacuum | 0 | ≤ 3e-3 / 7e-4 / 3e-5 | ≤ 1e-3 / 1e-4 / 1e-5 |\n\nThe even-bridge structure constants come out right through the limit for every state, including the $0\\cdot\\infty$ singlets at L = 2, where $\\langle W^L|\\Psi\\rangle\\sim\\varepsilon^2$ and $K/N\\sim\\varepsilon^{-2}$. At L = 3, $C_2=C_4$ on all states. The L = 2 targets agree with the table in `ABJM-3pt-transfer-matrices.md` §5.7 ($C_2=-1/\\sqrt{40}$, $1/\\sqrt{24}$). The L = 3 values were computed from scratch in python and have not been compared with field C of the data file.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Rerun 2026-10-13 (Wolfram, complex128, L = 2 only; 158 s).** Reproduced: $|$RHS − LHS$|\\le 5\\times10^{-7}$ throughout (machine cancellation at small $\\varepsilon$); $|\\langle\\Psi_0|\\Psi_\\varepsilon\\rangle|\\to1$; $|$RHS − target$|$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-2},10^{-3},10^{-4}$: singlet E=20 (target −0.158114): mode vac 1.60e-3 / 1.58e-4 / 1.6e-5, mode shift 5.2e-4 / 5.3e-5 / 4.8e-6; singlet E=4 (target |0.204124|): vac 2.0e-3 / 2.0e-4 / 2.0e-5, shift 7.0e-4 / 6.8e-5 / 6.8e-6; [1,0,1] pair (target 0, both conjugate states): vac 5.4e-3 / 5.4e-4 / 5.4e-5, shift 3.1e-3 / 3.1e-4 / 3.1e-5; vacuum (target 1): vac 2.7e-13 / 2.8e-11 / 3.8e-9, shift 8.5e-12 / 6.5e-10 / 1.0e-8 (python: 3e-13 / 3e-11 / 1e-8 and 4e-12 / 2e-10 / 7e-8; same order, the vacuum error is rounding noise amplified by $K/N\\sim10^8$). All $O(\\varepsilon)$ as claimed.\n\nMinor: the sign of the E=4 singlet target is **−0.204124** in this port (phase of $\\Psi_0$ fixed by making its largest component positive), the python table quotes +0.204124 ($=1/\\sqrt{24}$). The comparison RHS − target uses the same phase, so the error column is unaffected. The weight-{1,1,−1,−1} sector also appears (RHS = target = 0).\n\n**SKIPPED (too heavy): the L = 3 rows of the table** (6 sites; `pgUntwist[3, ...]` was not run: a single 6-site transfer-matrix build takes more than 300 s and several GB in this port). Those claims are not reproduced in this rerun.",
